 <longdesc><para unique="1046139">Performs a floating-point scale of the scalar double precision floating-point value in the first source operand by multiplying it by 2 to the power of the double precision floating-point value in second source operand.</para>
  <para unique="1046140">The equation of this operation is given by:</para>
  <para unique="1046141">xmm1 := xmm2*2<superscript>floor(xmm3)</superscript>.</para>
  <para unique="1046142">Floor(xmm3) means maximum integer value &#8804; xmm3.</para>
  <para unique="1046143">If the result cannot be represented in double precision, then the proper overflow response (for positive scaling operand), or the proper underflow response (for negative scaling operand) is issued. The overflow and underflow responses are dependent on the rounding mode (for IEEE-compliant rounding), as well as on other settings in MXCSR (exception mask bits, FTZ bit), and on the SAE bit.</para>
  <para unique="1046144">EVEX encoded version: The first source operand is an XMM register. The second source operand is an XMM register or a memory location. The destination operand is an XMM register conditionally updated with writemask k1.</para>
  <para unique="1046147">Handling of special-case input values are listed in <link unique="1046146" linkend="&lt;c&gt;VSCALEFPD-Scale-Packed-Float64-Values-With-Float64-Values.fm#43524: 06_Table: Table 5-30. \\VSCALEFPD Special Cases" xrefstyle="TableNum">Table 5&#8209;37</link> and <link unique="1046150" linkend="&lt;c&gt;VSCALEFPD-Scale-Packed-Float64-Values-With-Float64-Values.fm#36948: 06_Table: Table 5-31. Additional VSCALEFPD/SD Special Cases" xrefstyle="TableNum">Table 5&#8209;38</link>.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <programlisting>SCALE(SRC1, SRC2)
{
	; Check for denormal operands
TMP_SRC2 := SRC2
TMP_SRC1 := SRC1
IF (SRC2 is denormal AND MXCSR.DAZ) THEN TMP_SRC2=0
IF (SRC1 is denormal AND MXCSR.DAZ) THEN TMP_SRC1=0
/* SRC2 is a 64 bits floating-point value */
DEST[63:0] := TMP_SRC1[63:0] * POW(2, Floor(TMP_SRC2[63:0]))
}</programlisting>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1046164">VSCALEFSD (EVEX encoded version)</title>
   <programlisting>IF (EVEX.b= 1) and SRC2 *is a register*
	THEN
		SET_ROUNDING_MODE_FOR_THIS_INSTRUCTION(EVEX.RC);
	ELSE
		SET_ROUNDING_MODE_FOR_THIS_INSTRUCTION(MXCSR.RC);
FI;
IF k1[0] OR *no writemask*
	THEN DEST[63:0] := SCALE(SRC1[63:0], SRC2[63:0])
	ELSE
		IF *merging-masking*								; merging-masking
			THEN *DEST[63:0] remains unchanged*
			ELSE 							; zeroing-masking
				DEST[63:0] := 0
		FI
FI;
DEST[127:64] := SRC1[127:64]
DEST[MAXVL-1:128] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>VSCALEFSD __m128d _mm_scalef_round_sd(__m128d a, __m128d b, int);
VSCALEFSD __m128d _mm_mask_scalef_round_sd(__m128d s, __mmask8 k, __m128d a, __m128d b, int);
VSCALEFSD __m128d _mm_maskz_scalef_round_sd(__mmask8 k, __m128d a, __m128d b, int);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046187">Overflow, Underflow, Invalid, Precision, Denormal (for Src1).</para>
  <para unique="1046188">Denormal is not reported for Src2.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046193">See <link unique="1046191" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#63155: 06_Table: Table 2-47. Type E3 Class Exception Conditions" xrefstyle="Table All - no page with period">Table&#160;2&#8209;49, &#8220;Type E3 Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
